window.__finlexDocLoaded(10178,{"id":10178,"articles":[{"id":1000743,"no":"Overview","heading":"Scope & Statutory / Regulatory Role (Public Summary)","text":"Authorizes the IRS to reallocate gross income, deductions, credits, or allowances between commonly controlled entities to prevent tax evasion or clearly reflect income, anchored in the Arm's Length Standard and Best Method Rule.","seq":0},{"id":1000744,"no":"IRC §482 / Reg. §1.482","heading":"Best Method Rule, Commensurate-with-Income & Cost Sharing","text":"• Best Method Rule (Treas. Reg. §1.482-1(c)): Select the transfer pricing method (CUP, Resale Price, Cost Plus, CPM, Profit Split) providing the most reliable measure of an arm's length result.\n• Commensurate with Income (CWI) Standard: For transfers/licenses of intangible property, income must be 'commensurate with the income attributable to the intangible' (allowing periodic IRS adjustments).\n• Penalties & Documentation (IRC §6662(e)): Contemporaneous transfer pricing documentation required to avoid 20%/40% valuation misstatement penalties; Advance Pricing Agreements (APAs) available.","seq":1},{"id":1000745,"no":"Cross-Framework Comparison","heading":"US vs. International (ISA/OECD/COSO) & China Context","text":"• Broadly aligned with the OECD Transfer Pricing Guidelines (CPM ≈ TNMM), though US Reg. §1.482-7 Cost Sharing Arrangements (CSAs) and the statutory 'commensurate with income' rule have distinct US litigation history.","seq":2},{"id":1000746,"no":"Official Access","heading":"Official Regulatory / Statutory Source","text":"Official Source (Office of the Law Revision Counsel (U.S. Code)): https://uscode.house.gov/\nStatus: in_force.","seq":3}]});
